window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"camille","b":"zaahen","win":["Skill","Camille","Camille","Skill","Skill","Camille","Camille"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3","text":"Hookshot opens trades but The Darkin Glaive into Aureate Rush answers back, both 10s to your 16s — timing decides it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"The Hextech Ultimatum isolates him, but Grim Deliverance heals him and full Determination revives."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Trinity plus Precision Protocol's true damage tips long duels your way — bring Grievous Wounds for his heals."},{"when":"Late","text":"Split-push Camille out-duels him 1v1 — the sidelane becomes your kingdom and he has to answer it."}],"wants":{"you":["Punish his whiffed cooldowns","Scale evenly to Trinity","Sidelane 1v1s after one item"],"foe":["Punish whiffed Hookshots","Bank Determination stacks off you","Group to dodge your split"]},"early":"A genuinely even bruiser lane through 1-5: matched Q trades at 2, and at 3 Hookshot lands but The Darkin Glaive into Aureate Rush answers it back. Both are 10s to your 16s, so he is never out of cooldowns. He punishes overextension; you punish a whiffed 14s Dreaded Return. Keep trades short — Cultivation of War banks Determination off every hit he lands.","mid":"Level 6 stays even — The Hextech Ultimatum isolates him, but a 110s Grim Deliverance heals him through your burst and full Determination revives him, so treat ult fights as coinflips. The split comes at Trinity: your spike plus true damage tips extended duels your way. Bait the 14s Dreaded Return, then take the long trades.","late":"Two-plus items you want the side lane, but earn it: The Darkin Glaive heals him every 10s and Grim Deliverance heals again, so Grievous Wounds makes the duel yours. Push him to tower, take the fight when he answers alone, and close with Hookshot off terrain — but check his Determination bar first.","whys":["Level 1 is even — both of you farm with nothing online and no combo worth forcing.","Level 2 stays even: matched Q trades with no clear favourite, so keep it to short honest exchanges.","Level 3 is even — Hookshot opens trades but a 10s Darkin Glaive into Aureate Rush answers straight back for free.","Levels 4-5 stay a skill window: he punishes overextension, you punish every whiffed cooldown. Discipline decides each trade.","At 6 it's still even — The Hextech Ultimatum isolates him, but Grim Deliverance heals him back and full Determination revives him.","First item is Camille's: the Trinity spike and true damage tip extended duels your way. Start taking the long fight.","Two-plus items are yours — split-push Camille out-duels him 1v1, so plant your flag in the sidelane and make him answer it."]});
